A||N||9||AusFiero||Large K Size Image Posts - Some of are on modem connections||||13||
Z||000000||AusFiero||08-05-2001||08:53 AM||||Ok I notice around the forum that some of the images posted are ridiculously large in K size. Someone  even justified it with saying High resolution or nothing. Well that might work in theory but you gotta remember the net runs at 72 DPI so posting your 600 DPI images and above makes them no clearer online.<P>It would be nice to consider that some of us do not have access to cable connections. For instance the other night before it is as big as it is now I decided to let the Pics of Our Cars thread load in a window while I had dinner. It took 20 minutes due to just 1  image being over 700K in size and was way to big to fit on screen anyway, and I run at 1024 X 768. I pity those at 800X600 trying to view those threads.I took that image across into my computer and reduced it to 52 K without losing any resolution.<P>Come on guys, have some consideration for people using 800X600 (the webs most popular resolution currently) and particularly some consideration for those that cannot get or do not have a cable connection. That 1 image was larger than some 10 page websites I have built. I fit in the first group, I do not have access to cable, as much as I would like to. <P>If you want to run images that size why not post a smaller version and put a link to the so called high resolution version on your own server or homepage. At least that gives people an option if the want to see it bigger, because lets face it not may people run their screen size at the 1600X1200 needed to keep that image on screen.<P>Cliff, Is there anyway you can put a limit on the K size of files being uploaded to your server as it only takes 1 image like that to kill a thread for a lot of users?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||13
Z||000001||chester||08-05-2001||11:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Ok I notice around the forum that some of the images posted are ridiculously large in K size. Someone  even justified it with saying High resolution or nothing. Well that might work in theory but you gotta remember the net runs at 72 DPI so posting your 600 DPI images and above makes them no clearer online.<P>It would be nice to consider that some of us do not have access to cable connections. For instance the other night before it is as big as it is now I decided to let the Pics of Our Cars thread load in a window while I had dinner. It took 20 minutes due to just 1  image being over 700K in size and was way to big to fit on screen anyway, and I run at 1024 X 768. I pity those at 800X600 trying to view those threads.I took that image across into my computer and reduced it to 52 K without losing any resolution.<P>Come on guys, have some consideration for people using 800X600 (the webs most popular resolution currently) and particularly some consideration for those that cannot get or do not have a cable connection. That 1 image was larger than some 10 page websites I have built. I fit in the first group, I do not have access to cable, as much as I would like to. <P>If you want to run images that size why not post a smaller version and put a link to the so called high resolution version on your own server or homepage. At least that gives people an option if the want to see it bigger, because lets face it not may people run their screen size at the 1600X1200 needed to keep that image on screen.<P>Cliff, Is there anyway you can put a limit on the K size of files being uploaded to your server as it only takes 1 image like that to kill a thread for a lot of users?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree. I used to be on DSL but now back to 56K and it does get trying at times to read some of the threads.  <IMG SRC="http:/