Z||000002||stimpy||08-05-2001||11:31 AM||||Sad fact, Aus, but people are inconsiderate and they don't care a rats ass about the technological limitations of others.  I've been commenting about this type of bandwidth abuse for a while, only to get shot down every time. They can do it, so they will. And if your technology can't cut it, you shoulda upgraded.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||08-05-2001||11:50 AM||||pretty much if a thread says pics or it has more than 3-4 pics i just wait and see if i get a chance to see it at work. i don't complain much because i guess thats the price or tradeoff i pay by using such a simple internet device ($50 refurb webtv). but if others with fuller systems are having trouble also i'll cast my lot with them and request lower resolution pics too. maybe i'll see a little more.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||08-05-2001||12:04 PM||||Cast my lot with Aus & Stimpy. It's one of the reasons I didn't post in 'pics of people behind our cars', or a sig pic. I haven't figured out how to make it small enough. Aus, at least when you showed us the large pics of your 'other car' you made an apology and explained why it was that way. Do thumbnails take just as long to load?||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||08-05-2001||12:16 PM||||thumbnails if done right are almost instantaneous , Mind you though you can still post a pic 500 X 400 odd pixels and keep it down to 20 odd K. 700 or more than half a meg when you put it in perspective is just way over the top. As Stimpy said, people just say upgrade. Well umm I run a Pentium 3 800 EB with 256 meg of ram and a64 meg 3d video card. Unfirtunately like many around the world and a lot of America I just don't have access to cable even though I want it. <P>Will maybe have access to sattelite connection late this year. At least it is quicker. Not quite cable but quick.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||08-05-2001||12:45 PM||||Part of the problem may be that people don't know how to make a picture smaller before posting. Any of you image gurus out there care to take a stab at a FAQ on resizing an image (resolution and kb)???||||reg||3
Z||000007||Monkeyman||08-05-2001||12:50 PM||||I agree.  Before trying to downsize the pics, maybe some could crop the pics 1st.  I've seen tons of pics that have more meaningless background than anything.  Can you do thumbnails on the forum?  If so, someone let me know how and I'll do that for all of my pics from now on.  I think that's a great idea.  If I ever get a web site started (only been working on that off and on for the past couple of years with no progress yet), I could post a small pic here with a link to the full size one.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||08-05-2001||01:00 PM||||I would love too, only one problem. Most people have different software. All the large posts come from quality digital cameras usually. I know mine can shoot 2600X1800. If it is a quality camera it always comes with software of some kind for editting. It only takes a few minutes to search the help files in any given program to learn how to do it as it usually a pretty easy process with any image editting software. If no software there is actually plenty of image resizers available at places like <A HREF="http://www.tucows.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tucows.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.freeware.com" TARGET=_blank>www.freeware.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.downloads.com." TARGET=_blank>www.downloads.com.</A> <P>They will do the job for you and many are free.||||reg||1
Z||000009||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-05-2001||07:29 PM||||I agree completely.<P>I used to have DSL before we moved to the country..now I have a 33.6 connection.<P>I find some of these threads take forever(and some are near impossible to load)..<P><BR>I agree, a  size limit should be put into effect..easier on Cliffs server also.<P>The thumbnails or links are a great idea.<P><BR>||||reg||9
